ebohse ). But the addition, \"for those who had driven him into banishment,\" does not suit the latter and less memorable occasion: for Miriam and Aaron did but \"speak against Moses,\" not attempt to banish or expel him. More fully expressed, the meaning may be, \"For a people who began by making him a fugitive, Ex. ii. 15, Acts vii. 29, and now had put the finishing stroke to their ingratitude.\" Comp. Ex. xvii. 4; Num. xiv. 10, Num. xiv. 13, etc."},{"id":"4a91932b75f0","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":10,"p":[9,9],"r":[14,10],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"uper twn fugadeusantwn auton . When the \"intercession\" of Moses is spoken of, it is natural to suppose that the reference is to Exod. xxxii. 11 ff. But Sav. and Ben. refer this to Num. xii. 13, perhaps because of eboa (LXX. ebohse ). But the addition, \"for those who had driven him into banishment,\" does not suit the latter and less memorable occasion: for Miriam and Aaron did but \"speak against Moses,\" not attempt to banish or expel him. More fully expressed, the meaning may be, \"For a people who began by making him a fugitive, Ex. ii. 15, Acts vii. 29, and now had put the finishing stroke to their ingratitude.\" Comp. Ex. xvii. 4; Num. xiv. 10, Num. xiv. 13, etc."},{"id":"3b279ad9c6ee","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":10,"p":[9,9],"r":[14,13],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"uper twn fugadeusantwn auton . When the \"intercession\" of Moses is spoken of, it is natural to suppose that the reference is to Exod. xxxii. 11 ff. But Sav. and Ben. refer this to Num. xii. 13, perhaps because of eboa (LXX. ebohse ). But the addition, \"for those who had driven him into banishment,\" does not suit the latter and less memorable occasion: for Miriam and Aaron did but \"speak against Moses,\" not attempt to banish or expel him. More fully expressed, the meaning may be, \"For a people who began by making him a fugitive, Ex. ii. 15, Acts vii. 29, and now had put the finishing stroke to their ingratitude.\" Comp. Ex. xvii. 4; Num. xiv. 10, Num. xiv. 13, etc."},{"id":"4855df7f55c0","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":14,"p":[2,2],"r":[11,16],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Num. xi. 16"},{"id":"4fe3125b8b4a","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":14,"p":[2,2],"r":[11,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Num. xi. 14"},{"id":"368fc89d1126","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":17,"p":[5,5],"r":[12,3],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Num. xii. 3"},{"id":"0ffead90b530","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":18,"p":[5,5],"r":[15,32],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Num. xv. 32"},{"id":"10bc67598cf8","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":34,"p":[5,5],"r":[12,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Num. xii. 14"},{"id":"f155393df0d9","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":46,"p":[2,2],"r":[6,1,6,21],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"This vow appears to have been the Nazarite vow described in Num. vi. 1-21, taken by the apostle as an accommodation to Jewish prejudices and to allay the suspicions of the legal party in Jerusalem. This was done upon the recommendation of James, the \"Bishop\" of the church, and his associates. The significance of Paul's paying the expenses, is, perhaps, that the period during which the others vow had run was on this condition reckoned to his account also. It is noticeable that the party of James distinctly admits that adherence to the legal ceremonies is not required of the Gentile Christians; it is equally important to notice that Paul yielded to the advice to take this view, as a concession in a matter of indifference, since he was living for the time as a Jew among Jews, that he might give no needless offence and might win the more. It was not a compromise, but an expedient concession to convictions and prejudices which it was not wise or necessary to oppose or increase.-G. B. S."},{"id":"a12c1b45313c","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_rom","w":"chrysostomus.hom_rom","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":10,"p":[29,29],"r":[11,5],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Num. xi. 5"},{"id":"ac5edc7d494c","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_rom","w":"chrysostomus.hom_rom","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":16,"p":[37,37],"r":[24,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Numb. xxiv. 9"},{"id":"b8f26450688c","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_rom","w":"chrysostomus.hom_rom","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":30,"p":[28,28],"r":[10,29],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Num. x. 29"},{"id":"c56a8200ea29","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_1co","w":"chrysostomus.hom_1co","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":1,"p":[14,14],"r":[12,3],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Numbers chapter 12, verse 3"},{"id":"5bb5a2a1b142","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[38,38],"r":[15,32],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Num. xv: 32"},{"id":"ca3606720e12","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[38,38],"r":[15,36],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Num. xv: 36"},{"id":"e1696aaf7dbe","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":7,"p":[21,21],"r":[31,47],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Num. xxxi: 47"},{"id":"9975d8e7028e","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_eph"